{
  "info": {
    "title": "Ozone Connect - Bank Products Data",
    "contact": {
      "name": "Ozone Financial Technology Limited"
    },
    "description": "This document provides an API description in [OpenAPI](https://spec.openapis.org/oas/v3.0.1.html)\nfor Bank Product Data APIs for Ozone Connect.\n\nThese APIs should be implemented by an financial institution so that Ozone\ncan expose the API operations to TPPs.\n\n#### Implementer Notes\n\nImplementers should note that this API prescribes a positive response for correctly executed\noperations including those where no data is returned. This is consistent with the general principles\nof REST.\n\nPlease refer to the API Hub documentation for details of test cases that are \navailable for this API using the Ozone Connect test suite.\n\n### Versioning\n\nThe `version` property implements the following pattern `{standards-major}.{standards-minor}.{ozone-connect-version}`, where:\n\n* `standards-major` is the major version of the latest UAE standard that the API description implements.\n* `standards-minor` is the minor version of the latest UAE standard that the API description implements.\n* `ozone-connect-version` is the version of the Ozone Connect API description.\n\nSo, for example, `v2.0.1` indicates the first version of the Ozone Connect API description that implements the UAE standard version 2.0.\n**Please adhere to the deprecated flags in your implementation. Do not implement deprecated properties when** **implementing new functionality.**\n### v2.2.2\n* Changed `post /leads` to constrain the personal-data fields it accepts. `Data.EmiratesId` on both the request\n  and the response now carries `pattern: ^784-?[0-9]{4}-?[0-9]{7}-?[0-9]{1}$`, matching the Emirates ID pattern\n  already used by the Insurance API descriptions. Per OFP-009.\n\n* Changed `GivenName`, `LastName` and `FullName` on `AEUserName` to accept Latin letters, space, apostrophe,\n  period and hyphen only, and `BusinessName` to accept those plus digits, ampersand, comma, parentheses and\n  forward slash. Field lengths are unchanged. Per OFP-009.\n\n* Changed `AddressLine` on `AEResidentialAddress` to accept the ISO 20022 `PostalAddress27` `x` character set,\n  as already applied to the reference fields in the Bank Service Initiation API description. Field lengths and\n  item counts are unchanged. Per OFP-009.\n\n### v2.2.1\n* Added new version compatible with v2.2 of standards\n* Changed `get /products` to return `ExpectedProfitRates`, providing one-or-more deposit rates for\n  Sharia-compliant products. Each rate carries `RateType` (`FixedProfit` or `VariableProfit`),\n  `DepositRateType` (`ExpectedProfitRate` or `IndicativeProfitRate`), `ProfitSharingRatio`,\n  `ProfitDistributionMethod`, `ProfitDistributionFrequency`, an optional `Description`, and `RateDetails`.\n\n* Changed `get /products` to return `ShariaFinanceRates`, providing one-or-more finance rates for\n  Sharia-compliant products. Each rate is discriminated on `RateType` as a fixed profit rate, a variable\n  profit rate or a hybrid profit rate, and carries `ProfitCalculationMethod` with the values\n  `PrincipalBalance`, `OutstandingBalance`, `InitialDrawdownAmount`, `UnusedCreditLine` or `UtilizedLimit`.\n\n* Changed `get /products` to return `TakafulRequired`, indicating whether Takaful coverage is required for\n  the product, and `TakafulDescription`, describing the type and purpose of the required coverage.\n\n* Changed `get /products` to return `ProfitCalculationMethod` on charge components, for use in place of\n  `InterestCalculationMethod` where the product uses Islamic calculation methods.\n\n* Changed `InterestCalculationMethod` on charge components returned by `get /products` to apply to interest\n  only. Islamic calculation methods are now described by `ProfitCalculationMethod`.\n\n* Changed `RateDetails` on the deposit rates returned by `get /products` to reference a shared Schema Object,\n  so that the same rate structure is used by both `DepositRates` and `ExpectedProfitRates`. No change to the\n  properties returned.\n",
    "version": "v2.2.2"
  },
  "servers": [
    {
      "url": "https://[Ozone_Connect_API]"
    }
  ],
  "source_path": "/leads",
  "operations": {
    "post": {
      "tags": [
        "Leads"
      ],
      "summary": "Create a Lead",
      "description": "Create a Lead\n",
      "operationId": "CreateLead",
      "parameters": [
        {
          "$ref": "#/components/parameters/providerId"
        },
        {
          "$ref": "#/components/parameters/callerOrgId"
        },
        {
          "$ref": "#/components/parameters/callerClientId"
        },
        {
          "$ref": "#/components/parameters/callerSoftwareStatementId"
        },
        {
          "$ref": "#/components/parameters/apiUri"
        },
        {
          "$ref": "#/components/parameters/apiOperation"
        },
        {
          "$ref": "#/components/parameters/callerInteractionId"
        },
        {
          "$ref": "#/components/parameters/ozoneInteractionId"
        },
        {
          "$ref": "#/components/parameters/x-fapi-customer-ip-address"
        }
      ],
      "requestBody": {
        "description": "Request Body\n",
        "content": {
          "application/json": {
            "schema": {
              "$ref": "#/components/schemas/LeadRequest"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "responses": {
        "201": {
          "$ref": "#/components/responses/201LeadResponse"
        },
        "400": {
          "$ref": "#/components/responses/BadRequestResponse"
        },
        "401": {
          "$ref": "#/components/responses/NotAuthorizedResponse"
        },
        "403": {
          "$ref": "#/components/responses/ForbiddenResponse"
        },
        "500": {
          "$ref": "#/components/responses/InternalServerErrorResponse"
        },
        "default": {
          "$ref": "#/components/responses/errorResponse"
        }
      }
    }
  },
  "security": [
    {},
    {
      "OzoneConnectApiKey": []
    },
    {
      "OzoneConnectClientCredentials": [
        "placeholder"
      ]
    },
    {
      "OzoneConnectJwtAuth": []
    }
  ],
  "securitySchemes": {
    "OzoneConnectApiKey": {
      "description": "Communications between the API Hub and the LFI Ozone Connect implementation are secured using an API Key, which is a secret shared between the API Hub and the LFI.",
      "type": "apiKey",
      "in": "header",
      "name": "Authorization"
    },
    "OzoneConnectClientCredentials": {
      "type": "oauth2",
      "description": "Communications between the API Hub and the LFI Ozone Connect implementation are secured using a Client Credentials grant type.\n\nLFIs must host an OAuth 2.0 Authorization Server to utilise this security pattern. Scope values are set during the onboarding process, and represented by a placeholder in this API description.\n",
      "flows": {
        "clientCredentials": {
          "tokenUrl": "https://example.lfi.ae/token",
          "scopes": {
            "placeholder": "Placeholder for scopes, which are set by the LFI during onboarding"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "OzoneConnectJwtAuth": {
      "description": "Communications between the API Hub and the LFI Ozone Connect implementation are secured using the \"JWT Auth\" mechanism, where the Client presents a signed JSON Web Token as a credential.\n\nThe Server MUST verify the signature in order to authenticate the Client.\n\nPlease note that the value of the `scheme` parameter is not a registered HTTP Authentication Scheme, to indicate it is specific to Ozone Connect. Please refer to API Hub documentation for further details.\n",
      "type": "http",
      "scheme": "Ozone-Connect-JWT-Auth"
    }
  }
}

{
